+ version: "1.1.0"
+ description: "A complete podcast launch kit covering show concept, format design, equipment, scripting, recording, editing, hosting, directory submission, launch assets, and sustainable growth."
+ Podcast Launchpad is your end-to-end guide for creating and launching a podcast. It walks you through every phase — from raw idea to published episode — with actionable frameworks, gear recommendations, script templates, launch assets, distribution strategy, and QA checks. Whether you are a solo creator or building a team show, this skill provides the structure you need.
+ - **Directory submission:** Apple Podcasts, Spotify, YouTube Music, Amazon Music, Overcast, Pocket Casts, Castbox, and platform-specific directories relevant to the audience
+ - **Verification note:** Directory rules and platform names change over time; verify current submission requirements before telling the user a listing is available or complete.
+ Launch asset checklist:
+ - Show title, subtitle, category, language, explicit-content setting, and short/long descriptions
+ - Cover art direction, file requirements, alt-text, and brand-safe color notes
+ - Trailer outline, episode 1 outline, and two follow-up episode briefs
+ - Guest invitation template, release/consent reminder, and recording checklist
+ - Show notes template with timestamps, links, credits, and accessibility notes
+ - Directory submission tracker with status, submission URL, approval date, and known blockers
+ - Launch QA checklist covering RSS validation, loudness target, metadata, artwork, links, and playback test
+ - Do not claim a podcast has been accepted by, ranked on, or monetized through any platform unless the user provides current evidence.

